WEBVTT

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:37.410
July, 1999. The world will be destroyed.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.770
I don't believe the prophecy,

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.480
but I can't deny that some weird stuff
is happening at the academy.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.530
If that perverted loser is entrusted
with the fate of the world,

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.080
we're all as good as doomed!

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.260
If the prophecy is true,
the only one who can stop it is-

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.720
Maya-san!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.180
My glasses! My glasses!

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.400
Kozue?

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.360
What has you all riled up this morning?

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.510
A spoon?

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.520
I'm sorry.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.970
I wanted to show it to
you as soon as I could.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.820
You're not going to tell me you've gotten
into bending spoons, too, are you?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.750
No.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.810
It's something even more amazing!

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:30.930
A spoon that never rusts!

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.880
It must be an OOPArt, don't you think?

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:14.070
The term "OOPArt" refers to objects
of unknown origin or manufacture,

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.290
or whose creation would be impossible

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.990
given a civilization's relative level,
for a certain time.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:23.030
However, the vast majority of
publicly announced OOPArts

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.480
have been fakes or misunderstandings.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.960
The Iron Pillar of Delhi, for example,

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.340
famous for never rusting, was simply covered
with iron oxide, preventing rust.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.070
In other words, this is just a spoon.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.800
1995?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.070
It's brand-new...

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.080
It's not an OOPArt!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.390
Got it?

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.700
Yes!

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.980
I'll go find something else!

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.010
Hey, hasn't Kozue been acting weird lately?

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.630
She's always weird.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.520
This is a girl who stands under
waterfalls as a hobby.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:09.610
Man, I've got a feeling I'm
gonna get called on.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.270
Kozue, you got the textbook?

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.730
First period is...

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:19.000
Now then, open your textbook to page 44...

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.000
Kumashiro.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.830
Actually, let's go with Kuroki.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.700
Me?

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.960
Wow, you're a prophet!

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.620
Jeez, bad feelings are always
the accurate ones.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:33.580
Loser.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.480
Did something happen with Abe?

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.480
What do you mean by "something"?

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.350
You looked unbelievably pissed.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.840
He try to hit on you?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.140
Or the opposite?

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:48.110
Lending a hand to help out
the new teacher, principal?

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.050
No.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.860
By the way, where's Kozue?

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.590
How far is she going in search
of those OOPArts?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.110
Big problems!

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.400
That's what I was about to say...

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.540
What happened?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.470
First, look at this!

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.100
A spirit photograph!

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.980
See these orbs?

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.560
Orbs?

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.790
The ones that are supposed to
be human souls or emotions?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.510
Yes, that's right!

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.520
It's just light, reflected
off the dust in the air.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.320
You can't be sure!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.000
Then let's take a look.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.260
You're standing near a waterfall, aren't you?

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:37.000
Reflections like this occur more often
when the air is moist.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.360
The vast majority of spirit photography
is just bad photography.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.750
So what happened?
You're hurt.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.430
Oh, yeah...

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.670
A black cat crossing your path is bad luck.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.540
A chance to see if it's true!

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.360
Wait!

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.010
A kitty!

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:35.780
It crossed my path!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.620
It was true...

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.530
That doesn't even qualify as "occult."

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.780
And you forced it into doing it, too.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:52.710
Some countries say that's a sign
of good luck, you know?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.070
Which is true?

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.290
I know! I can prove whether
it's good or bad luck...

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.730
How?

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.400
With something like Russian Roulette?

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.480
You'll die for sure!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.350
No, Wasabi Russian Roulette!

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:12.860
You get a bunch of pastries and
hide wasabi in one of them!

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.410
Oh, yeah. The ones you use
in a punishment game?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.830
Kozue always gets that one.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.700
Then that's not gonna work.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.490
Take your seats.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.270
I'll find something else for you!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.780
And so then, in other words...

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.100
A poltergeist?

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.530
No, it's just an earthquake.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.450
Excuse me, sensei!

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.380
Are those runes?
Some kind of lost language?

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.480
Or are you actually an alien?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.950
No, he's just got bad handwriting...

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.710
One, two, three...

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.110
One, two, three...

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.120
Look!

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.210
It's a tsuchinoko!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.010
<b>Minorun'chi</b>

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.350
Abe-sensei, you have a visitor.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.960
I'll be right there!

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.090
Perk up, you guys.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.860
How can you be perky
after all that running?

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:40.990
Yes... The path to the occult
is long and hard.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.970
A scoop!

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.270
Now what?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.120
You want to sell at the school?

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.820
Yeah. I was hoping I could sell some
snacks on school grounds.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.720
Just running a restaurant
isn't enough to get by.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.480
Times are hard...

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:01.410
No. I have to pay off my car loan.

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:15.090
Yeah... Bread made by someone in
the local town won't be very good.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:35.580
If you're going to sell it to students,

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:38.270
you may want to make the
taste a bit stronger.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:39.720
Right!

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.150
I'll ask about selling on school grounds.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.710
Really?

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.860
If we could eat your bread every day,

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.980
I... Everyone would be really happy, I think.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.560
Thank you!

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:07.010
Um... Can I get you to taste it again?

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:08.780
O-Of course!

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.780
Ten or twenty! However many...

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.010
Maya-san!

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.680
One, two, three!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.560
What?

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.480
You've never heard of the
three-second rule?

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.190
If you pick it up within
three seconds, it's fine!

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:43.720
Another superstition?

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:47.050
And why were you screaming
all of a sudden?

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.140
Oh, the noon program today was about
strange mysteries of the world!

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:52.540
I forgot!

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:56.770
Human-faced sheep, people living at the
South Pole, a real pushmi-pullyu!

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.980
I wanted to see it so bad...

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.290
You done already?

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.720
I'm full.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.530
If you sleep after you eat,
you'll turn into a cow!

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.210
Really?

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:12.730
Ow.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.190
Ow!

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:19.390
Kozue, you're going a bit nuts
with this "occult" thing.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:20.550
Did something happen?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.370
No, not a thing.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.520
That's the problem.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:29.200
I'm the only person in this school

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.720
who's never had an occult experience.

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:33.040
Sure you have!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.430
You got turned into a departed spirit,
kidnapped by tengu...

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.530
But I didn't see those.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.630
I see.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.830
"What's important are the things
you can't see with your eyes."

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.250
What's that from?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:44.780
<i>The Little Prince.</i>

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.280
What everyone searches for can be found

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.970
in a single rose or a small bit of water.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.830
But you can't see it with your eyes.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.270
You need to see with your heart.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.460
I guess my heart just isn't there yet.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.260
That's why I can't find it.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:05.240
But I'll do my best, and someday...

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.430
It's gonna get hotter.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.940
Is that a prophecy?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.040
Everyone knows it.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:31.520
Ventura, Ventura, space people!

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.820
Don't call them!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:44.060
Page 51 in your textbooks...

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.470
Kumashiro,

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.510
put the book away,
and take out your textbook.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.540
Hey, Kumashiro!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.300
We'll go with Kuroki actually!

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:56.240
Again?

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.760
You suck, Abe.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.520
Stop failing.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.810
You hate him that much?

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.690
Don't even want to talk about him.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.830
Is Kozue not here today?

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.960
Dunno. Haven't heard from her.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:19.610
I figured she'd bring me something again,
first thing this morning.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.250
Maybe she's learned better.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.120
Not a chance.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:27.900
Someone's calling me.

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.650
It's a phone. They do that, yeah.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.130
Hello?

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.850
Turn the power off.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:46.370
The teachers will take it.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.260
You, too.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.340
It's from Kozue.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:53.560
Don't look for me?

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.780
She's vanished?

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:58.230
I'm going to become a god.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.410
That girl again...

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.190
Hey... Wait.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.490
This is #6.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.880
The simulator has been destroyed,

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:11.180
so I'm reporting in with #5's phone,
which I recovered.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:12.070
Liar!

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:12.930
I'm sorry!

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:16.690
A civilian, in possession of the
historical change simulator...

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.100
This is unheard of!

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:21.990
Suppose she changes the future
with that technology?

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:25.150
But that's why I'm here, isn't it...

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.150
Number 6!

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:27.220
I'm sorry!

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.890
And you're no closer to finding the key!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.000
Work harder!

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.820
The future of the world depends on you.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.020
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.600
"Sorry" won't save the world.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.270
Right. You're right.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:43.520
Don't forget.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.250
There's no time.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:48.790
July, 1999.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:51.580
A Great King of Terror
will come from the sky...

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.370
Find the Key of Nostradamus.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.440
X-Day is...

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.760
July 21st.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:00.900
Abe-sensei!

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.630
Sensei, Kozue is...

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.620
You don't need to come.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:07.410
What the heck?

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.760
<b>Home Ec Prep Room</b>

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.900
Oh, are you angels?

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.810
You look like Ami-san and Maya-san.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.500
What are you doing in here again?

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.090
It smells like vinegar.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.660
I was about to see something...

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.470
From starvation.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.610
Sokushinbutsu...

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:37.660
That's the spiritual training where you
go underground while still alive, right?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.690
Yup.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:40.500
Kozue does it all the time.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.490
And she always ends up
smelling like vinegar.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:44.290
Not always!

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.460
Last time, I smelled like plum sake.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.120
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:51.760
You got drunk off the smell.
It was pretty bad.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:55.050
How's Naruse?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.530
She's calmed down.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:59.020
We're okay here.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:08.650
Please.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.820
No.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.540
Let her sell stuff off a wagon?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.650
Right after this happened
to one of your students?

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.080
I promised Mikaze-san!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.120
I'm not leaving till you say yes.

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:22.370
Please.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.010
We're looking for the key together, right?

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.480
I'm done with that.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.710
What? You were the one
who said we'd work together, Maya-

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.430
Don't say my first name.

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:33.450
What if someone heard you?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:36.800
You're a teacher.
People would think something's up.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.740
Something?

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.100
Oh, I see.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.370
No way.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.850
I've never been even remotely
interested in you that way...

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:47.520
We're done!

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:49.520
<b>Approved</b>

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:51.530
Yes.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.030
Thank you, Abe-sensei!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:58.700
What's wrong?

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:02.750
No, um... Just kinda hurt is all.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.830
Oh, should I call a doctor?

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:10.900
I'm fine.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.660
It's nothing.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.270
I see.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.320
Hurt, hurt, go away!

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:29.430
It's a spell to make it better.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:41.230
I was wrong to work with him!

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:44.010
I never trusted him from the start!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.610
Then let's experience it for ourselves.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:48.770
Who wants to volunteer?

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:49.580
Scary.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.350
You do it.

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:51.140
No!

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:53.860
I'll do it!

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:54.330
Kozue?

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:55.350
Naruse?

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.800
Isn't it dangerous?

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.780
You?

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:01.800
Yes! I want to have
a near-death experience!

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:05.240
People who get lost in the snow

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:09.360
have been discovered without pulse or respiration,
but were successfully revived.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.470
This has occurred several
times throughout history,

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:13.230
and we're going to recreate
that process here.

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:16.030
All men die.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:18.610
But what happens afterwards?

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:23.000
By undergoing a virtual death experience,
she'll be able to glimpse the other world.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.300
The time limit is exactly 3:00 minutes.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:30.180
Any more or less, and it increases
the dangers of revival.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.510
Yes.

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.380
Kozue...

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.500
Be careful.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.160
Right!

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.220
I'll go see it for myself!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.010
13 degrees, 12.4 degrees, 12.1 degrees...

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:59.720
Heart rate 174. 70...

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.830
It's kind of cold.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.440
My arms won't move...

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.280
My head is heavy, too...

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:13.350
Dad... Mom...

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:15.750
Thank you for everything.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:21.430
Big Sis... Even in the afterlife,
I won't forget what you did with my pudding.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:39.280
This is the afterlife?

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.210
Are there aliens or something?

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.350
What religion was Naruse-san again?

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:42.550
I can't see a thing!

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.230
I wonder if my grandmother's there.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.330
My body is light!

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.160
Because I'm a soul?

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:14.750
This is water?

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.720
Maybe the river Styx?

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.660
Can I drink it?

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:19.470
Drink it!

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.590
No!

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.340
Kozue.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:52.760
It's time.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:20:59.850
It's calling me.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:01.250
I have to go back.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:19.130
Welcome back!

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:22.170
You feel enlightened?

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.190
Where are your glasses?

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:31.670
I don't need them.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:36.670
How was it?

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:37.860
What?

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.150
Your near-death experience.

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:45.540
Near-death experience?

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:49.370
Aw, that's just silly occult stuff.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:22:06.480
My glasses... My glasses... My glasses... My glasses...
My glasses... My glasses... My glasses... My glasses...

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:10.540
My glasses!

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:13.950
My glasses!

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.260
This is Naruse Kozue.

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:51.120
I'm trying my first preview.

00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:53.380
Next time on <i>Occult Academy</i>:

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:56.590
Occult? Seriously?

00:23:56.590 --> 00:23:58.510
What's wrong, Kozue?

00:23:58.510 --> 00:24:00.550
Next time on <i>Occult Academy</i>:

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:02.300
BUNMEI's distance.

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:04.680
Don't you read those last two kanji "virgin"?

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:06.050
It's "distance."

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:07.230
Normally, it's "virgin."

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:08.320
No, it's "distance" here.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:09.050
Virgin.

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:09.640
Distance.

00:24:09.640 --> 00:24:10.100
Virgin.

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:10.700
Distance.

00:24:10.700 --> 00:24:11.210
Distance.

00:24:11.210 --> 00:24:14.740
Virgin... The occult is so naughty!

00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:19.800
This program is a work of fiction.
Departed spirits, psychic abilities,
aliens, UMAs, etc., do not exist.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:19.800
Unless you believe in them...
